essary for the website to function and is used specifically to collect user personal data via analytics, ads, other embedded contents are termed as non-necessary cookies. It is mandatory to procure user consent prior to running these cookies on your website.	[Semiconductor Engineering] Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastructure Home > Low Power-High Performance > Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastr. Low Power-High Performance WHITEPAPERS 112G PHY IP for linear optics t...	PUBLISHED	2026-08-13 12:29:48.256121+05:30	\N	\N	110	254	2026-08-13 12:32:03.56482+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.105432+05:30	\N	1	https://semiengineering.com/standards-compliant-112g-phy-for-linear-optics-driving-efficient-ai-infrastructure/	Semiconductor Engineering	[Semiconductor Engineering] Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastructure Home > Low Power-High Performance > Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastr. Low Power-High Performance WHITEPAPERS 112G PHY IP for linear optics t...	### Event Overview\n[Semiconductor Engineering] Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastructure Home > Low Power-High Performance > Standards-Compliant 112G PHY for Linear Optics: Driving Efficient AI Infrastr Low Power-High Performance WHITEPAPERS 112G PHY IP for linear optics to reduce power, latency and thermal load for high-speed data movement in AI and data center systems August 12th, 2026 - By: Synopsys Linear optics are the path to scaling AI interconnects beyond 800G — cutting DSP and retimer overhead to reduce power, latency, and thermal load.\n\n### Context & Technical Summary\nSynopsys has developed the industry’s first 112G PHY IP compliant with OIF-CEI-112G-LINEAR-PAM4, with measured TX/RX results meeting and in several cases exceeding the spec Download the white paper for full characterization data What you’ll learn: - Why linear optics matter now — up to 50% module power savings and lower thermal load in dense AI racks - What OIF-CEI-112G-LINEAR-PAM4 standardizes — a repeatable, interoperable ecosystem - How Synopsys 112G PHY performs — TX VMA, jitter, eye-closure, and RX JTOL against CEI limits - What this unlocks — DSP-less host-to-module connectivity, scalable to 224G/448G and CPO Read more here.	["• Low Power-High Performance WHITEPAPERS 112G PHY IP for linear optics to reduce power, latency and thermal load for high-speed data movement in AI and data center systems", "• August 12th, 2026 - By: Synopsys Linear optics are the path to scaling AI interconnects beyond 800G — cutting DSP and retimer overhead to reduce power, latency, and thermal load", "• Synopsys has developed the industry’s first 112G PHY IP compliant with OIF-CEI-112G-LINEAR-PAM4, with measured TX/RX results meeting and in several cases exceeding the spec", "• Download the white paper for full characterization data", "• What you’ll learn: - Why linear optics matter now — up to 50% module power savings and lower thermal load in dense AI racks - What OIF-CEI-112G-LINEAR-PAM4 standardizes — a repeatable, interoperable ecosystem - How Synopsys 112G PHY performs — TX VMA, jitter, eye-closure, and RX JTOL against CEI limits - What this unlocks — DSP-less host-to-module connectivity, scalable to 224G/448G and CPO Read more here"]	Detailed technical breakdown across 2 dynamic sections.	Advances in VLSI SEMICONDUCTOR directly impact system engineering workflows. Tracking general updates enables engineers to optimize architectural decisions and mitigate operational risks.	For SIET engineering students: Reviewing this case study offers practical grounding in General concepts, real-world deployment patterns, and industry best practices.	vlsi-semiconductor	General	["VLSI SEMICONDUCTOR", "General"]	18	https://semiengineering.com/standards-compliant-112g-phy-for-linear-optics-driving-efficient-ai-infrastructure/	Semico