Intel may be heading back to memory	intel-may-be-heading-back-to-memory	Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan (pictured) is teasing a return for Intel to the memory market.\n”I used to be, ‘do not invest in memory because it is a kind of commodity business,’ but now it has become different,” Tan said on a TechSurge podcast, , “there is a lot of new technology coming out. So, we are kind of looking at one of my pet projects, some of the new memory architecture. I think you just saw the news: I hired my good friend, Seok-Hee Lee, who used to run SK Hynix. So, you kind of know something that I am thinking about. We are not ready to unfold it.”\n“ I think CPU and memory, I think there are a lot of ways we can really do stacking together,” Tan said. “And also try to find some new architecture for memory. I think in some way the memory, a lot of innovation are not there. So, ured) there is some really good area.”\nTan has mentioned that stacking memory on top of a CPU could make a lot of sense.\nAn Intel XBM patent that does away with the silicon interposer of HBM filed December 2024 and published the patent describes a “cross-batch memory (XBM) with backend transistors” to replace HBM.\nIntel also has a jv research intiative called Saimemory with a number of Japanese partners to develop Z-angle memory (ZAM),	Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan (pictured) is teasing a return for Intel to the memory market	PUBLISHED	2026-08-13 09:35:03.750456+05:30	\N	\N	116	147	2026-08-13 09:35:03.758114+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.13997+05:30	\N	1	https://www.electronicsweekly.com/news/business/intel-may-be-heading-back-to-memory-2026-08/	Electronics Weekly	[Electronics Weekly] Intel may be heading back to memory Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan (pictured) is teasing a return for Intel to the memory market. ”I used to be, ‘do not invest in memory because it is a kind of commodity business,’ but now it has become different,” Tan said on a TechSurge podcast, , “t...	### Event Overview\n[Electronics Weekly] Intel may be heading back to