Everything Announced At The VR Games Showcase - August 2026	everything-announced-at-the-vr-games-showcase-august-2026	Looking for all of the new game reveals and announcements from today's VR Games Showcase? Read on for a full recap.\nThe showcase, hosted by Jamie Feltham, featured over twenty-five games with new reveals, release dates, fresh content and more. You can watch the full show on the VRGS YouTube channel.\nHere's the full rundown, starting with the main show.\nNew Game Reveal - Total Chaos VR\nLeading today's VR Games Showcase, developer Trigger Happy Interactive and publisher Apogee Entertainment have announced that Total Chaos VR is coming to SteamVR soon. A standalone version of the game is also coming to Meta Quest. The PC VR version will be free for anyone who already owns the flatscreen Steam game.\nBootstrap Island Out Now On PlayStation VR2\nWe called Bootstrap Island a sterling VR survival adventure and rated it four out of five stars when it went to the final 1.0 release. Now after months of waiting, PlayStation VR2 gets the full game with all post-release content.\nGunman Contracts Will Launch With Steam Frame\nThe action movie inspired first person shooter Gunman Contracts Stand Alone will launch in Early Access on the same day as Steam Frame. The exact release date for Valve's headset and now this game is still unknown.\nNew Game Reveal - Tiny Flock\nNo Brakes Games, the maker of Human Fall Flat, announced Tiny Flock, a made-for-VR physics-based puzzle game coming to Steam and Meta Quest.\nOut Of Sight VR Release Windows For PS VR2 & Meta Quest\nExpect Flat2VR's Little Nightmares-like horror title Out of Sight VR this holiday season for PlayStation VR2 and in 2027 for Meta Quest.\nLearn More About Drifters: Blackout Crew\nDrifters: Blackout Crew, first revealed in the summer edition of the VR Games Showcase, shared more info about the sci-fi co-op extraction shooter gameplay. \nIn case you missed it, check out our interview with Salmi Games' founder Yacine Salmi on the UploadVR Gamescast as well.\nNew Game Reveal - Spirit Ritual\nSpirit Ritual is a terrifying ghost story, played in either mixed reality or virtual reality, that blends full motion video with mixed-reality gameplay. It is coming to Pico, PC VR, and Meta Quest.\nAll On Board Adds A New FREE Game Next Week\nSocial board game app All On Board is adding a new game, Virus!, as a free update next week.\nR.A.I.D. Drops New Gameplay Trailer & Pre-Order Bonus\nCo-op sci-fi shooter R.A.I.D. from FusionPlay and Impact Inked has opened pre-orders ahead of its upcoming release. In R.A.I.D., you inspect interstellar cargo ships to catch smugglers. If the cargo comes up nefarious, you board the ship for high-octane shootout action.\nCOVR Unveils First Official Trailer\nWe got a new look at COVR, a tactical mil-sim first person shooter from XReal Games (Zero Caliber).\nZero Caliber 2 Hits PS VR2 This October\nSpeaking of XReal Games, its action-packed cinematic shooter Zero Caliber 2 finally arrives on PlayStation VR2 this October.\nGreen Hell VR Painting Update\nHardcore survival adventure Green Hell VR adds more customization with today's Modular Buildings & Painting update. With the new Painting system, players will be able to craft a brush and bowls of paint, then add some color to the structures around the camp. Modular building has also been expanded with triangle frames and new plank structures, opening up even more possibilities for new builds.\nThe new update is available on Meta Quest and PS VR2.\nAnother Look At The Lightkeepers & Price Reveal\nCo-op exploration and survival adventure The Lightkeepers launches on September 10 on Meta Quest and with today's new video, we know the price will be $19.99.\nA New Look At Adrian's Quest\nAdrian's Quest is one of our most anticipated upcoming games in 2026. We got a fresh look at the upcoming single-player action-adventure in a new trailer.\nA New Look At The Rifted Skies\nWe got a new trailer for The Rifted Skies, a physically demanding action-roguelike from location-based-entertainment developer DreamVR.\nCONVRGENCE Leaves Early Access Next Month\nPost apocalyptic extraction shooter CONVRGENCE leaves Steam Early Access on September 17.\nKnights Of Fiona Launch Date\nCo-op JRPG Knights of Fiona launches September 3 for Meta Quest and Steam. It has several playtest sessions happening over the next few days.\nNew Rustmourne Gameplay Trailer\nRustmourne was first announced in our UploadVR Summer Showcase in June and the VR Games Showcase premiered a new video showing more of the Dead Space-inspired gameplay. Expect Rustmourne on PC VR in early 2027.\nPayday: Aces High Launches Playtests Next Week\nFast Travel Games' co-op heist shooter Payday: Aces High kicks off live playtests on August 20.\nFlat2VR & Impact Inked To Bring More Games To PS VR2\nSoul Assembly's Drop Dead: The Cabin was the featured game in a brief video teasing a 'vault' of new titles coming to PlayStation VR2. The video featured Myles Dyer from Flat2VR, YouTuber Bryan Paul of Without Parole, and former Sony executive Shuhei Yoshida among others.\nTrombone Champ: Unflattened Disney DLC Coming Next Week\nNote: We were notified by VR Games Showcase host Jamie Feltham shortly before the showcase started that the Disney Movie Magic Vol. 1 DLC had been shifted to an August 20 release date. The showcase trailer said 'Out Now.' An amended trailer has since been published.\nFlat2VR Studios first announced the Disney Movie Magic DLC earlier this summer after a tease in the spring and next week you can play multiple tracks from classic Disney films in its premier rhythm game.\nFlat2VR Announces StartEngine Online Investment Campaign\nFlat2VR Studios announced a StartEngine online investment initiative to help expand its publishing portfolio and grow the internal teams needed to bring more VR ports and original games to market. We'll have a more in-depth story on this soon.\nNew Game Reveal - High On Life VR\nSpeaking of Flat2VR, they weren't done yet in this showcase. Squanch Games' comedic first person shooter High On Life is getting a VR port for PC VR, PlayStation VR2 & Meta Quest.\nNew Game Reveal - System Shock VR\nThe main show closed with the shocking reveal (pun fully intended) of Flat2VR's port of acclaimed 2023 sci-fi shooter System Shock. System Shock VR is also coming to PC VR, PlayStation VR2, and Meta Quest.\nPrior to the main show fronted by Feltham, a pre-show hosted by Zeena Al-Obaidi dropped announcements for six additional games.\nBrushHammer Gets A Release Date\nMixed reality miniature painting app BrushHammer Miniature Painter drops on Meta Quest on August 26.\nVertigo Rush Lays Out Its Launch Roadmap\nHigh speed VR racer Vertigo Rush charted its path to its planned Q4 2026 release in a new video.\nOmega Pilot: Evolution Out Now On PlayStation VR2\nAnother showcase shadow drop, futuristic Wipeout-inspired racer Omega Pilot: Evolution is available now on PS VR2.\nBattleGroupVR2 Launches On Meta Quest This Month\nSpace real-time-strategy game BattleGroupVR2 comes to Meta Quest in Early Access on August 28. It previously launched, also in Early Access, for SteamVR late last year.\nNew Game Reveal - Stuffed: Two Foot Hero\nWaving Bear Studio has announced Stuffed: Two Foot Hero, a new VR wave shooter coming to SteamVR and Meta Quest this fall.\nNew Game Reveal - Grablings: Paint N' Seek\nTriangle Factory and Triangle Labs have announced Grablings, a social hide and seek game coming to Meta Quest this summer.	[UploadVR] Everything Announced At The VR Games Showcase - August 2026 Looking for all of the new game reveals and announcements from today's VR Games Showcase. Read on for a full recap.	PUBLISHED	2026-08-14 03:56:30.948075+05:30	\N	\N	116	342	2026-08-14 03:56:41.093688+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.166103+05:30	\N	1	https://www.uploadvr.com/everything-announced-at-the-vr-games-showcase-august-2026/	UploadVR	[UploadVR] Everything Announced At The VR Ga