CAN XL transceiver supports data rates up to 20Mbps	can-xl-transceiver-supports-data-rates-up-to-20mbps	TI claims to have launched the industry’s first commercially available CAN XL transceiver with the TCAN6062 Controller Area Network extended data-field length (XL) transceiver.\nThe device supports payloads up to 2,048 bytes per frame and data rates up to 20Mbps, while ensuring that priority messages are delivered first and on time with the performance on which humanoid robots, industrial robots and human-machine interface (HMI) systems depend.\nThe TCAN6062’s backward compatibility with CAN flexible data rate (FD) and CAN signal improvement capability (SIC) operations enables seamless migration to CAN XL, allowing teams to evolve existing designs incrementally without requiring a full redesign.\nAdditionally, the transceiver allows engineers to consolidate communication layers and use Ethernet in mixed-network architectures with Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol (TCP/IP) tunnelling, enabling efficient transfers of diagnostics, sensor data, control traffic and over-the-air updates on a single network.\nNew networking requirements sometimes push engineers to accept system-level trade-offs to compensate for bandwidth constraints and the TCAN6062 aims to bridge that gap by offering a path to higher-bandwidth networks while maintaining the proven reliability if CAN,.\nThe TCAN6062 CAN XL transceiver’s SIC helps reduce ringing by as much as 80% in complex networks, simplifying validation in high-node architectures.\nCombined with wide input/output voltage compatibility and protection up to ±58V, the transceiver offers broad design flexibility across a range of industrial applications.\nSee all our Texas Instruments content.	[Electronics Weekly] CAN XL transceiver supports data rates up to 20Mbps TI claims to have launched the industry’s first commercially available CAN XL transceiver with the TCAN6062 Controller Area Network extended data-field length (XL) transceiver. The device supports payloads up to 2,048 bytes ...	PUBLISHED	2026-08-13 12:29:27.422289+05:30	\N	\N	117	246	2026-08-13 12:30:14.807628+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.100266+05:30	\N	1	https://www.electronicsweekly.com/news/products/can-xl-transceiver-supports-data-rates-up-to-20mbps-2026-08/	Electronics Weekly	[Electronics Weekly] CAN XL transceiver supports data rates up to 20Mbps TI claims to have launched the industry’s first commercially available CAN XL transceiver with the TCAN6062 Controller Area Network extended data-field length (XL) transceiver. The device supports payloads up to 2,048 bytes ...	### Event Overview\n[Electronics Weekly] CAN XL transceiver supports data rates up to 20Mbps TI claims to have launched the industry’s first commercially available CAN XL transceiver with the TCAN6062 Controller Area Network extended data-field length (XL) transceiver The device supports payloads up to 2,048 bytes per frame and data rates up to 20Mbps, while ensuring that priority messages are delivered first and on time with the performance on which humanoid robots, industrial robots and human-machine interface (HMI) systems depend The TCAN6062’s backward compatibility with CAN flexible data rate (FD) and CAN signal improvement capability (SIC) operations enables seamless migration to CAN XL, allowing teams to evolve existing designs incrementally without requiring a full redesign.\n\n### Context & Technical Summary\nAdditionally, the transceiver allows engineers to consolidate communication layers and use Ethernet in mixed-network architectures with Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol (TCP/IP) tunnelling, enabling efficient transfers of diagnostics, sensor data, control traffic and over-the-air updates on a single network New networking requirements sometimes push engineers to accept system-level trade-offs to compensate for bandwidth constraints and the TCAN6062 aims to bridge that gap by offering a path to higher-bandwidth networks while m