Walkabout Dungeon Golfer Officially in Production After Fake April Fools Reveal	walkabout-dungeon-golfer-officially-in-production-after-fake-april-fools-reveal	Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, initially presented as a fake April Fools Day game earlier this year, was formally announced in today's special Mighty Coconut Presents video.\nWe also got the course trailer for the upcoming Gloop Lair DLC, and news on Mighty Coconut branching into third-party game publishing.\nGame developers and other companies often get in on the April Fools Day fun with ridiculous announcements and updates, but sometimes the interest from the developer or the community is so strong that things get real. Such is the case with Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, a roguelike dungeon crawler Mighty Coconut teased.\nA few days later, Mighty Coconut updated with the following:\nWalkabout Dungeon Golfer was initially a joke, but we got excited about it the more time we spent with it! No promises, but we're starting to play with some prototypes.\nDuring the special presentation, Mighty Coconut founder Lucas Martell shared some concept art and more details about the game. Walkabout Dungeon Golfer will be a hybrid title with crossplay support for flatscreen and VR platforms. It uses the same physics engine as Walkabout Mini Golf with you and your friends putting through dungeons, fighting monsters, and leveling up abilities. Martell said the team does not have a release date, but the target is summer 2027.\nInterested players can subscribe to Mighty Coconut's Walkabout Connection newsletter for progress updates and any news on upcoming playtests here.\nOther Mighty Coconut Presents Announcements\nAdditionally, Martell also announced that Mighty Coconut will be publishing Grass, a flatscreen cozy co-op lawn mowing simulator from developer Cosmic Dog. You control a remote controlled mower. Grass can be wishlisted now on Steam and will also be available on Xbox.\nThe final announcement was the reveal trailer for this Thursday's Gloop Lair DLC course, introduced by Game Director Jeremy Wynn. Gloop Lair is part of the ongoing Evil Lairs series, a 90s metropolis whose entire water supply has been transformed into hazardous gloop.\nHere's the full trailer:\nThe full 'Mighty Coconut Presents' video is available on Mighty Coconut's YouTube channel. We'll share any additional news on Walkabout Dungeon Golfer as it comes along.	Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, originally an April Fools Day fake, is now officially in production as a hybrid title with both VR &amp; flatscreen support	PUBLISHED	2026-08-13 09:35:21.765408+05:30	\N	\N	117	179	2026-08-13 09:35:21.778585+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.282978+05:30	\N	1	https://www.uploadvr.com/walkabout-dungeon-golfer-officially-in-production-after-fake-april-fools-reveal/	UploadVR	[UploadVR] Walkabout Dungeon Golfer Officially in Production After Fake April Fools Reveal Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, initially presented as a fake April Fools Day game earlier this year, was formally announced in today's special Mighty Coconut Presents video. We also got the course trailer for th...	### Event Overview\n[UploadVR] Walkabout Dungeon Golfer Officially in Production After Fake April Fools Reveal Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, initially presented as a fake April Fools Day game earlier this year, was formally announced in today's special Mighty Coconut Presents video We also got the course trailer for the upcoming Gloop Lair DLC, and news on Mighty Coconut branching into third-party game publishing Game developers and other companies often get in on the April Fools Day fun with ridiculous announcements and updates, but sometimes the interest from the developer or the community is so strong that things get real.\n\n### Context & Technical Summary\nSuch is the case with Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, a roguelike dungeon crawler Mighty Coconut teased A few days later, Mighty Coconut updated with the following: Walkabout Dungeon Golfer was initially a joke, but we got excited about it the more time we spent with it No promises, but we're starting to play with some prototypes.	["• We also got the course trailer for the upcoming Gloop Lair DLC, and news on Mighty Coconut branching into third-party game publishing", "• Game developers and other companies often get in on the April Fools Day fun with ridiculous announcements and updates, but sometimes the interest from the developer or the community is so strong that things get real", "• Such is the case with Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, a roguelike dungeon crawler Mighty Coconut teased", "• A few days later, Mighty Coconut updated with the following: Walkabout Dungeon Golfer was initially a joke, but we got excited about it the more time we spent with it", "• No promises, but we're starting to play with some prototypes"]	Detailed technical breakdown across 2 dynamic sections.	Advances in AR VR XR directly impact system engineering workflows. Tracking general updates enables engineers to optimize architectural decisions and mitigate operational risks.	For SIET engineering students: Reviewing this case study offers practical grounding in General concepts, real-world deployment patterns, and industry best practices.	ar-vr-xr	General	["AR VR XR", "General"]	24	https://www.uploadvr.com/walkabout-dungeon-golfer-officially-in-production-after-fake-april-fools-reveal/	UploadVR	https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/2f/2a2f38f0-4b71-407a-9c7e-18a9e2541980/content/images/2026/08/walkaboutDungeonGolfer.png	\N	2026-08-13 09:35:21.778417+05:30	2026-08-13 09:35:21.778417+05:30	70aa0c0549ca907f9eb979ccfa786673c144c8dff2e2b46f0db68671c24eb5c1	\N	processed	1	single_source	[UploadVR] Walkabout Dungeon Golfer Officially in Production After Fake April Fools Reveal Walkabout Dungeon Golfer, initially presented as a fake April Fools Day game earlier this year, was formally announced in today's special Mighty Coconut Presents video. We also got the course trailer for th...	[{"heading": "Event Overview", "paragraphs": ["[UploadVR]