Arduino App Lab 0.10: Meet Agentic Mode	arduino-app-lab-010-meet-agentic-mode	Arduino App Lab 0.10: Meet Agentic Mode\nWe’re thrilled to announce Arduino App Lab 0.10, our biggest release yet. With this update, you can now build applications alongside an AI agent that actively works on your project, not one that just answers questions about it.\nPowered by MCP and integrated with App CLI, Agentic Mode understands your workspace, creates and edits files, runs your app, and interprets errors as they happen. It has deep knowledge of App Lab, Apps, Bricks, and Sketches.\nAlongside Agentic Mode, App Lab 0.10 also introduces Language Server support for code completion and navigation, a streamlined way to connect your board to Arduino Cloud and a restructured Examples library. Here’s a breakdown.\nThe big one: Agentic Mode\nAgentic Mode and session panel in Arduino App Lab 0.10\nOpen Arduino App Lab and you’ll notice a new button at the bottom of the screen “Agentic Mode.” Through its MCP integration with App CLI, it understands your workspace and actively works on your project.\nIf you need a reminder, MCP (Model Context Protocol) is an open standard that lets AI models interact with external tools and systems. Rather than just generating text, an MCP-connected agent can invoke tools, read state, and take actions, in this case, through Arduino App CLI.\nIt’s what allows Agentic Mode to go beyond simple conversation and actually operate on your project.\nAgentic Mode can create and edit files, run your App, stop it when needed, and interpret errors as they happen. Ask it to build a feature and you can watch it assemble the project step by step, instead of handing you a wall of code to copy and paste. Watch this demo as an example.\nAgentic Mode works on a Bring-Your-Own-Key basis: you authenticate with your AI provider of choice, keeping you in control of your API usage and costs. Claude is supported at first, with more providers coming soon.\nFaster code editing with Language Server Support\nArduino App Lab 0.10 integrates a Language Server (not available in SBC Mode on UNO Q) that brings IDE-quality features to your Sketches and scripts: autocomplete, auto-formatting, hover documentation, “go to definition”, and “find all references” work across Arduino sketches, Python, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\nThe new Language Server allows Inline code definition\nConnect your board to Arduino Cloud, right from Settings\nYou can now register your Arduino® UNO™ Q board with Arduino Cloud directly from the Settings page, no need to leave Arduino App Lab. Once registered, your board is ready for IoT-enabled Apps.\nProvision UNO Q for Arduino Cloud directly from the Arduino App Lab’s device settings page.\nA clearer path through Examples\nThe Examples catalog has been restructured into three tiers so you always know where to start and where to go next:\n1. Inspirations: more than examples, full blown Applications that showcase what the board can really do. \n2. Examples: the fundamentals, taught through focused topics like LEDs, matrices, and the Bridge API.\n3. Bricks Examples:  small, interactive apps that each focus on a single Brick’s functionalities, so you can see one building block in action at a time.\nNew inspiration page to show the full potential of Arduino UNO Q\nDownload Arduino App Lab 0.10\nUpdate Arduino App Lab to 0.10.0.\nFor the full list of changes, see the release notes.\nResource\n- Purchase the Arduino UNO Q.\nArduino and UNO are trademarks or registered trademarks of Arduino S.r.l.	We&#8217;re thrilled to announce Arduino App Lab 0	PUBLISHED	2026-08-13 09:35:24.106536+05:30	\N	\N	116	191	2026-08-13 09:35:24.109992+05:30	2026-08-14 11:19:13.221919+05:30	\N	1	https://blog.arduino.cc/2026/08/12/arduino-app-lab-0-10-meet-agentic-mode/	Arduino Blog	[Arduino Blog] Arduino App Lab 0. 10: Meet Agentic Mode Arduino App Lab 0.	### Event Overview\n[Arduino Blog] Arduino App Lab 0 10: Meet Agentic Mode Arduino App Lab 0 10: Meet Agentic Mode We’re thrilled to announce Arduino App Lab 0.\n\n### Context & Technical Summary\n10, our biggest release yet With this update, you can now build applications alongside an AI agent that actively works on your project, not one that just answers questions about it Powered by MCP and integrated with App CLI, Agentic Mode understands your workspace, creates and edits files, runs your app, and interprets errors as they happen.	["• 10: Meet Agentic Mode Arduino App Lab 0", "• 10: Meet Agentic Mode We’re thrilled to announce Arduino App Lab 0", "• 10, our biggest release yet", "• With this update, you can now build applications alongside an AI agent that actively works on your project, not one that just answers questions about it", "• Powered by MCP and integrated with App CLI, Agentic Mode understands your workspace, creates and edits files, runs your app, and interprets errors as they happen"]	Detailed technical breakdown across 2 dynamic sections.	Advances in IOT directly impact system engineering workflows. Tracking general updates enables engineers to optimize architectural decisions and mitigate operational risks.	For SIET engineering students: Reviewing this case study offers practical grounding in General concepts, real-world deployment patterns, and industry best practices.	iot	General	["IOT", "General"]	27	https://blog.arduino.cc/2026/08/12/arduino-app-lab-0-10-meet-agentic-mode/	Arduino Blog	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558346490-a72e53ae2d4f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80	\N	2026-08-13 09:35:24.109724+05:30	2026-08-13 09:35:24.109726+05:30	9b2d7ff32e6d453db4a06c7f5c7170850416d59dcf2a3b0ffd9b6b33452c387c	\N	processed	1	single_source	[Arduino Blog] Arduino App Lab 0. 10: Meet Agentic Mode Arduino App Lab 0.	[{"heading": "Event Overview", "paragraphs": ["[Arduino Blog] Arduino App Lab 0 10: Meet Agentic Mode Arduino App Lab 0 10: Meet Agentic Mode We’re thrilled to announce Arduino App Lab 0."]}, {"heading": "Context & Technical Summary", "paragraphs": ["10, our biggest release yet With this update, you can now build applications alongside an AI agent that actively works on your project, not one that just answers questions about it Powered by MCP and integrated with App CLI, Agentic Mode understands your workspace, creates and edits files, runs your app, and interprets errors as they happen."]}]	full	f	\N
